      "attempt_count": 1,
      "asr_text": "For an hour, he sat listening while I stood completely still. Finally, he groaned softly, in fear, not pain. I knew that sound well. I opened the lantern's cover, sending light onto his eye. It was completely open now. I heard low, quick beats, like a watch wrapped in cotton. His heart grew faster and louder. What if a neighbor heard? I rushed to him, and he gave one scream. I pulled him down and covered him with the heavy bed. Finally, his heart stopped, and I could feel no pulse. I hid his body under three floorboards, then replaced them exactly. You could search all night and find no mark. At four that morning, three police officers arrived and knocked. A neighbor had heard a scream from the house.",
